{"schema_version":"1.9.2","id":"CLSA-2026-1793105895","published":"2026-10-27T12:58:27Z","modified":"2026-11-27T16:30:17.003061056Z","upstream":["CVE-2026-19630","CVE-2026-94300","CVE-2026-96888","CVE-2026-97313"],"summary":"Fix CVE(s): CVE-2026-19630, CVE-2026-94300, CVE-2026-96888, CVE-2026-97313","details":"   * SECURITY UPDATE: named could terminate unexpectedly when concurrent\n     messages signed or verified with the same GSS-TSIG key raced on its\n     shared security context\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-94300.patch: serialize access to the shared\n       GSS-TSIG security context (upstream dcb8b7cbc7)\n     - CVE-2026-94300\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: a resolver with a redirect zone and\n     qname-minimization strict could abort while processing the redirect\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-96888.patch: handle qname-minimization\n       failures when redirecting, and clear the AD flag on a redirect\n       NXRRSET (upstream b1bb41767d, 60dc845e57)\n     - CVE-2026-96888\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: a crafted DNS message could make named spend\n     disproportionate CPU time following chains of compression pointers\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-19630.patch: limit how many compression\n       pointers a name and a message may make named follow (upstream\n       d3cd0a1387); keeps the budget out of struct dns_decompress to keep\n       the libdns ABI\n     - CVE-2026-19630\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: a recursive resolver with two RPZ zones of different\n     recursive-only settings could abort on a non-recursive query that\n     followed a recursive one\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-97313.patch: only restore the recursionok\n       flag after RPZ-initiated recursion when the client asked for and\n       may have recursion (upstream 6823773725)\n     - CVE-2026-97313","affected":[{"package":{"name":"bind9","ecosystem":"TuxCare:Debian:11","purl":"pkg:deb/tuxcare/bind9?distro=debian-11"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"1:9.16.50-1~deb1